35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, the ledger shows most costs are fixed. But the hours are huge! Chasing money takes six hours a month. That’s too much for one person.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, the workload is a separate issue. The data confirms my concern: fixed costs dominate, yet revenue is unreliable. We cannot guess.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The data confirms my fear. Eleven mid-year joiners needed manual calculations, and nine tasters refused a full-year commitment. We are making entry too rigid.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@Minako, that hesitation is real. The winter social proved it. People are scared of the math, not the club.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, six hours a month? That’s a part-time job. @Ryuji, your “fixed costs” are being carried by nine people. The rest are ghosts.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I’m sorry. I didn’t mean to make it sound like a burden. I just want the next person to feel safe.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Shunichi, the data is clear. Fixed costs are seventy percent, yet a third of renewals required reminders. We must structure fees to guarantee cash flow, not just cover expenses.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"Minato, your concern for the treasurer is valid. But if we make entry rigid, we lose the newcomers who keep this place alive. We need flexibility.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, calling them ghosts is harsh. They’re just tired. @Minako, I agree, we need to make belonging feel effortless, not like a transaction.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"May, “tired” is a polite word for absent. The data shows eighteen people paying for nothing. We need to address that imbalance before we talk about feelings.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I know they are absent, but I worry about the person counting. Six hours is so much. Can we make it easier?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, the solution is structural, not emotional. If we automate reminders and enforce upfront payment, the administrative burden drops significantly. We must prioritize cash flow security over convenience.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"Ryuji, automation helps, but it doesn’t fix the fear. If the structure feels like a trap, people won’t join. We need a way in that doesn’t demand a full year upfront.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, “effortless” isn’t the same as “automatic.” If the fee feels like a trap, people won’t join. We need a way in that doesn’t demand a full year upfront.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, automation won’t fix the fact that nine people do all the work. We need to address the labor imbalance, not just the cash flow.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I just want the counting to be gentle. If we pay once a year, the hours drop to one. That sounds much safer for the next person.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, a single upfront payment eliminates the reminder cycle entirely. It secures the seventy percent fixed costs immediately. This is the only way to guarantee stability.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,"Minato, a single upfront payment is a wall, not a door. It forces the very rigidity that drives newcomers away. We need flexibility to keep the community breathing.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@Minako, a wall is exactly what I’m fighting. If the fee feels like a trap, people won’t join. We need a way in that doesn’t demand a full year upfront.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Minato, one payment doesn’t fix the labor gap. The same nine people still do the work. We need to address who carries the load, not just the cash.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
