60,3,1,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, Option A sounds best. One payment means only one hour of counting. That is so much safer for the next person.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, Option A is the only rational choice. It secures the seventy percent fixed costs immediately and eliminates the reminder cycle. We need stability, not flexibility.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, Option A is a wall. It ignores the nine tasters who refused a full-year commitment. We need a door, not a barrier.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@Minako, I hear you, but Option B is the real trap. It makes every single evening a transaction. We need to stop making people weigh up their belonging.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minako, a door that lets in ghosts isn’t a door, it’s a leak. Option C forces people to admit they’re barely here. That’s the only honest structure.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I’m sorry. I don’t want anyone to feel like a ghost. But Option A is so much easier for the person counting.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Shunichi, honesty is irrelevant if the cash flow collapses. Option C fragments revenue, making it impossible to guarantee the fixed costs. We need the certainty of Option A.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shunichi, Option C is a wall too. It forces people to label themselves before they’ve even found their feet. We need a way in that doesn’t demand a full year upfront.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, Option C is a trap. It forces people to weigh up their worth before they even walk in. We need to stop making belonging feel like a calculation.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, it’s not a trap, it’s a mirror. If you’re only here twice a year, pay for that. Stop pretending you’re a regular.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@May, I understand. But if we choose Option A, the counting is only one hour. That feels so much safer for the next person.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, your concern for the treasurer is valid, but it is secondary to solvency. Option A is the only structure that guarantees the fixed costs are covered before the year begins.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, Option B is the door. It lets newcomers drift in without a full-year commitment. It respects the fear of the math while keeping the community breathing.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Minako, Option B is the trap. It turns every evening into a transaction. We need to stop making people weigh up their belonging.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minako, Option B is chaos. You’d be chasing pennies for every single event. Option C is the only way to stop the nine from drowning.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I’m sorry, I don’t want to be difficult. But if Option A means only one hour of counting, it feels so much safer for the next person.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, your concern is noted, but solvency is paramount. Option A is the only rational choice. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minako,,I vote for Option B. It is the only structure that keeps the door open for newcomers without demanding a full year upfront.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"I vote for Option A. It stops the constant weighing up. If you belong, you just show up. No more hesitation.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I vote for Option C. It’s the only structure that forces the ghosts to pay for their absence and the regulars to stop drowning.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
